The examples you give are indeed equivalent, since they don't have enough
structure to show a difference, but at least the aspectuals do involve scope
considerations:

        mi ba'oku naku citka le plise
        I am in the aftermath of not eating the apple.
        (i.e. I am eating it.)

        mi naku ba'oku citka le plise
        I am not in the aftermath of eating the apple.
        (i.e. I have not eaten it.)

